# Canonical set of files the dictator MUST have to RUN + ACTUATE. Single source of truth, read by:
#   - sync-standby.sh   : which plain config/secret files to replicate primary -> warm standby
#   - cluster-doctor.sh : presence assertion (a dictator-capable box missing a critical file FAILs)
#
# This file exists because of the 2026-06-24 cutover incident: control_secrets.yaml was never
# sneakernet'd to 210, so the controller booted, decided OFF, but couldn't ACTUATE the Midea
# (issuer returned unknown-device) until a real state change exposed the gap. Enumerating the set
# here — and asserting it — means a future failover/rebuild can't silently lose control again.
#
# One row per file:  relpath | criticality | disposition
#   criticality:  critical = control/actuation breaks without it   | optional = degrade-only
#   disposition:  sync        = replicated standby<-primary by sync-standby (mutates on the primary)
#                 preposition = must already exist on BOTH boxes; NEVER sent over the wire (root trust)
#                 local       = box-local, not replicated (e.g. creds for a box-local broker)
#
# NOTE: the live state DBs (instance/db/control.db, mesh.db) are NOT listed here — they need a
# consistent sqlite snapshot and keep their bespoke handling in sync-standby.sh.

instance/.master_pass         | critical | preposition
instance/node_secrets.enc     | critical | sync
instance/control.yaml         | critical | sync
instance/control_secrets.yaml | critical | sync
instance/midea-device.env     | critical | sync
instance/mqtt.env             | optional | local
# Area taxonomy + device rename/relocate authoring state (ADR-0026) and the house-geometry /
# location-crosswalk source docs. SYNC 210 -> 245 so a promoted standby renders rooms + resolves
# device->area identically (mount-210-data / house-geo-backup-sync). optional = these are ingest/
# render inputs; control + actuation are unaffected if absent on the standby.
instance/areas.yaml           | optional | sync
instance/area-migration.yaml  | optional | sync
instance/device-rename.yaml   | optional | sync
instance/house-geometry.html  | optional | sync
instance/location-crosswalk.html | optional | sync
# ADR-0026 Phase-3 room-graph inputs for /api/v1/rooms (D1001 house-map + PWA). SYNC so a promoted
# standby serves the same rooms (geometry + per-device placement) — else the panel map degrades on failover.
instance/house-geometry.json  | optional | sync
instance/device-placement.yaml | optional | sync
# Device registries — raw device identity -> canonical device_id/area, read by the ingest mappers
# (edge_mapper, tasmota_bridge, levoit_bridge) + device_registry. SYNC so a promoted standby OR A NEW
# SERVER maps readings identically (added when airgap_router_pm S31 was inducted, 2026-07-06). optional =
# ingest degrades to unmapped readings if absent; control/actuation are unaffected (control.yaml owns those).
instance/devices.yaml         | optional | sync
instance/tasmota-devices.yaml | optional | sync
instance/levoit-devices.yaml  | optional | sync
# R9 (ADR-0017) HTTPS + web-push. SYNC (not local) on purpose: same cert + VAPID key on both boxes means
# a failover keeps the SAME self-signed cert (the browser's one-time trust survives) AND — decisive — the
# SAME VAPID key, because a push subscription is bound to the server key; a different key on the promoted
# standby would silently break every existing subscription. Optional = web-push/HTTPS degrade only; the
# plain :8123 + control/actuation are unaffected if absent. push_subscription rows ride control.db's snapshot.
instance/tls/server.crt       | optional | sync
instance/tls/server.key       | optional | sync
instance/vapid.json           | optional | sync
